# Rates

**Acme Studio \| autumn delivery programme and agreed rates**

The quarter covers eight workstreams for four clients. Hourly rates and fee envelopes are agreed before work starts; the project review tracks billable effort against the commissioned budget. Amounts are dollars.

Internal reviews, rework and proposal development are recorded but not charged. Changes to scope require client approval rather than automatic billing.

| @meta |                 ||                    | {:,.2f} {::>} | {:.1f}       |                |        |
|       | Project         || Client             | Hourly rate   | Budget hours | Purchase order | Terms  |
| ----- | --------------- || ------------------ | ------------- | ------------ | -------------- | ------ |
|       | Discovery       || Acme Manufacturing | 110           | 70           | PO-26-410      | Net 30 |
|       | Service design  || Acme Services      | 125           | 65           | PO-26-411      | Net 30 |
|       | Data migration  || Acme Cloud         | 140           | 80           | PO-26-412      | Net 30 |
|       | Portal delivery || Acme Distribution  | 150           | 95           | PO-26-413      | Net 30 |
|       | Reporting       || Acme Manufacturing | 130           | 65           | PO-26-414      | Net 30 |
|       | Training        || Acme Services      | 105           | 55           | PO-26-415      | Net 30 |
|       | Launch support  || Acme Cloud         | 160           | 75           | PO-26-416      | Net 30 |
|       | Retainer        || Acme Distribution  | 115           | 60           | PO-26-417      | Net 30 |



# Sessions

**Delivery time ledger \| September–November 2026**

The ledger records 120 delivery sessions, including two out-of-hours launch handovers. Billable time follows the approved project scope; internal review time is retained for utilization and margin analysis.

Managers review the ledger before invoices are released. Sessions crossing midnight remain assigned to the month in which the work began.

